<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=sail">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sail</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th millennium BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A sail is a tensile structure of fabric or another membrane that uses the wind to propel a craft; sailing boats appear on Cucuteni–Trypillian ceramics from the 6th millennium BCE, and excavations of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ubaid-period">Ubaid period</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> give direct evidence of them. When and where the sail was invented is not known. Sails are depicted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> around 3200 BCE, on reed boats sailing up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> against its current. Austronesian crab claw sails, used with outriggers and catamarans, carried settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sail.jpg" alt="Sail" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francis Christian Muller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chesapeake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>6th millennium BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Mesopotamia and eastern Europe</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Taiwan and Island Southeast Asia (Austronesian sails) (c. 3000 BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>When and where the sail was invented is not known; many date it no earlier than the 5th millennium BCE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/outrigger-canoe">Outrigger canoe<span>c. 3000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/trireme">Trireme<span>late 8th century BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/sternpost-rudder">Sternpost rudder<span>1st century CE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/lateen-sail">Lateen sail<span>2nd century CE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/windmill">Windmill<span>9th century</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/steamship">Steamship<span>1783</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=sail">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
